-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Jetpac
  Publisher   Ultimate, 1983
  Version     1.3

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Jet Pac (1983)(Ultimate Play The Game)(16K)[a2][a2].z80
  MD5         5875d535442974a0de82737652854f1f

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Jetman, the aliens, the rocket parts and the fuel in fuller
              multicolour. Source: enhanced colours from an older Spec256
              conversion (Spectrum Magic's jetpac_.zip), painter not
              established.

  Pace        original (-0.41% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless on the
              NextZXOS v2.09 card, against the plain build of the same file;
              probe 0x69C7 (the main loop's pass counter); Kempston replayed
              at the read 0x733C; R at 0x6602 and 0x69D0, the frame tick and
              the random byte at 0x69D8 fixed in both arms; 69 state addresses
              equal at every update)

  Changes     1.1: writes the whole alt ROM image (Sinclair's ROM plus the
              hooks), so the ROM's own interrupt code can never run the hooks.
              1.2: the hooks hand back the CPU speed the game was running at,
              instead of always dropping to 3.5 MHz
              1.3: the game holds the original's pace, where 1.2 ran about
              2.2% slower everywhere: a part of each figure's own set-up now
              runs at 28 MHz and pays for the sprite update's time.

  Note        Coloured build (not Dean's Jetpac build). Plays at the
              original's pace, measured with the same input and the same enemy
              choices in 5 runs of 1,000 game updates in JNext: overall -0.41
              to -0.16%, quiet scenes -0.51 to +0.32%, busy scenes -0.43 to
              -0.33%, slowest stretch of 20 updates +1.8%, fastest -2.1%;
              Enhanced overall -0.43 to -0.18%, slowest stretch +1.5%, fastest
              -2.4% (1.2 on the same runs: overall +2.11 to +2.34%, slowest
              stretch +4.0%; its earlier -0.6% had no state check). Known
              issues: the same keys can give different aliens from the
              unpatched conversion's, because this build reads Sinclair's ROM
              where that conversion reads NextZXOS's; the odds are the same,
              measured over 4,000 updates, and a real 48K Spectrum has
              Sinclair's. Missing: two-player games not checked; only level 1
              measured for pace; hardware untested.

